{"_about":"Even levels, the background measurer: the silence after each pass (evenlevels.cpp MEASURED gap), the early stop (MEASURED earlyStopDb) and the render speed. tools/soundlibraries/even_gap_check.py has the method, criterion and result. Measured 2026-10-13 on the Windows test VM: kthost (offline VST 3 host, a transport restart before each pass), Kontakt 8 + SSO, each Performance patch from MuseScore's resaved setup (library defaults: Tree mic + Leader as shipped), 44.1 kHz, the windows the background measurer renders of MuseScore's events (Recommended; Basses: Whence Celli bars 1-8 an octave lower). Per section and gap against 3 s, with the kthost process as the unit of noise: levels = each measured note's median-of-3-passes level per render, averaged per process (perceived, ~dB); fit = the glide fitted to it (dB); meanShift (SE, t), meanZ2 (bound: chi-square 95 %), rmsDiff / rmsNoise / effectRms; perRender: the same with the render as the unit (too strict: processes differ). selfCheck: the test within one gap (no effect). chosen: the smallest gap matching with every longer one. earlyStop: 2 passes, a 3rd only when a measured note differs by more than thresholdDb (95th percentile of |pass 1 - pass 2|), each render's fit against the other renders' 3-pass fits. tail: seconds after the last note-off until the power envelope stays below -40/-50/-60 dB re the measured notes' level (the envelope floors at -100 dBFS, so -50/-60 read as the gap itself). speed: per gap and section, and the sp_* checks (block size, idle, two processes at once) with their levels against the 3 s processes. Measurement only.","gaps":[0.25,0.5,1.0,1.5,2.0,3.0],"passages":{"W12C":{"route":"0-7","patch":"Celli - Performance","bars":4,"notes":64},"QC":{"route":"1-1","patch":"Celli - Performance","bars":8,"notes":120},"QV1":{"route":"0-4","patch":"Violins 1 - Performance","bars":8,"notes":56},"QVa":{"route":"0-11","patch":"Violas - Performance","bars":8,"notes":88},"QB":{"route":"1-1 -12","pa